<article class="env-lemma" id="0FWH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FWH">Lemma <span data-tag="0FWH">28.21.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a reduced scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Then the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/05P2" data-tag="05P2">28.21.2</a> are also equivalent to </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="(6)"><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite type and the function 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \rho _\mathcal {F} : X \to \mathbf{Z}, \quad x \longmapsto \dim _{\kappa (x)} \mathcal{F}_ x \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{X, x}} \kappa (x)  \]
</div>
<p>
 is locally constant in the Zariski topology on $X$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This lemma immediately reduces to the affine case. In this case the lemma is a reformulation of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FWG" data-tag="0FWG">10.78.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>